.TH DPEEK 1 "April 2026" "dpeek" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dpeek \- interactive terminal data viewer for CSV, TSV, JSON, and JSONL files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dpeek
[\fIflags\fR] \fIfile\fR
.br
\fIcommand\fR | \fBdpeek\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dpeek
is a TUI (terminal user interface) tool for interactively viewing and editing
data files directly in the terminal. It supports CSV, TSV, JSON, and JSONL formats.
.PP
CSV and TSV files are displayed as scrollable tables with cell editing, searching,
filtering, sorting, and column statistics. JSON and JSONL files are displayed as
collapsible trees with leaf editing and search.
.SH FLAGS
.TP
.B \-\-delimiter \fIchar\fR
Column delimiter for CSV files. Default: auto\-detected from file extension
(comma for .csv, tab for .tsv).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-header
Treat the first row as data instead of a column header.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.SS Navigation
.TP
.B \(ua/\(da/\(la/\(ra, h/j/k/l
Navigate cells or nodes.
.TP
.B PgUp/PgDn
Scroll one page up or down.
.TP
.B Home/End
Jump to first or last cell/node.
.SS Editing
.TP
.B Enter
Edit selected cell (CSV) or toggle/edit node (JSON).
.TP
.B Tab
Confirm edit and move to next cell/leaf.
.TP
.B Esc
Cancel edit, close overlay, clear search/filter, or quit.
.SS Features
.TP
.B F1
Toggle help overlay.
.TP
.B F2, Ctrl+S
Save file.
.TP
.B F3, /
Search. Prefix with \fB/\fR for regex (e.g. \fB/^foo\fR).
.TP
.B Ctrl+H
Search and replace. Uses the current search query; prompts for replacement text.
.TP
.B :
Open SQL query prompt (CSV/TSV only). The table is named
.BR data .
Press Esc or q to return to original data. Press : again to edit the query.
.TP
.B F4
Filter rows. Use \fBcol:value\fR to filter a specific column.
.TP
.B F5
Sort by current column (CSV only).
.TP
.B F6
Column statistics (CSV only).
.TP
.B Ctrl+G
Go to row, column name, or row:col (CSV). Go to node number (JSON).
.TP
.B n/N
Next/previous search match.
.TP
.B y
Copy cell value to clipboard.
.TP
.B p
Paste from clipboard.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Z
Undo.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Y
Redo.
.TP
.B e
Expand all nodes (JSON only).
.TP
.B c
Collapse all nodes (JSON only).
.SS Quitting
.TP
.B F10, q, Esc
Quit. Prompts for confirmation if there are unsaved changes.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Force quit without confirmation.
.SH SUPPORTED FORMATS
.TP
.B .csv
Comma\-separated values.
.TP
.B .tsv
Tab\-separated values.
.TP
.B .json
JSON files displayed as collapsible trees.
.TP
.B .jsonl
JSON Lines, each line parsed as an array element.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Open a CSV file:
.B dpeek data.csv
.TP
Open a TSV file:
.B dpeek data.tsv
.TP
Open a JSON file:
.B dpeek config.json
.TP
Open a CSV with a custom delimiter:
.B dpeek \-\-delimiter "|" data.txt
.TP
Open a CSV without headers:
.B dpeek \-\-no\-header raw.csv
.TP
Read from stdin:
.B cat data.csv | dpeek
